    "chunk_size_bytes": 1188,
    "chunk_text": "Key discussions will focus on promoting the growth and competitiveness of women-led SMEs, facilitating networking and knowledge sharing among entrepreneurs from Sri Lanka, India, Canada and other Indo-Pacific countries, and building strategic partnerships involving the private sector, government agencies, development organisations, financial institutions and international stakeholders.\n\nA significant outcome expected from the dialogue is the commencement of a consultative process to formulate a comprehensive Five-Year Strategy and Action Plan for Women\u2019s Development, Economic Empowerment and Women-Led SMEs in Sri Lanka.\n\nCanCham Sri Lanka noted that the proposed strategy would seek to create a stronger ecosystem for women entrepreneurs, improve access to markets and finance, and contribute to long-term economic resilience and inclusive prosperity.\n\nGPPAC multistakeholder forum at RCSS highlights climate-disaster vulnerability and need for community-centred solutions in Sri Lanka\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
