    "chunk_size_bytes": 911,
    "chunk_text": "These expeditions have ventured into little-known waters, revealing new insights into marine ecosystems, ocean processes, marine biodiversity, fisheries resources and the health of the Indian Ocean. It is a reminder that understanding this ocean is not merely a scientific pursuit but is essential to the food security and livelihoods of the millions of Sri Lankans who depend on the sea every day.\n\nThe speaker Dr. Prabath Jayasinghe, is the Principal Scientist and Head of the Marine Biological Resources Division at NARA. With over 25 years of research experience, he has led major national and international marine survey programs, represented Sri Lanka at the Indian Ocean Tuna Commission Scientific Committee, coordinated the Sri Lanka\u2013Norway Bilateral Fisheries Project, and authored more than 30 peer-reviewed scientific publications. The lecture is supported by Nations Trust Bank and is open to all."
