    "chunk_size_bytes": 1349,
    "chunk_text": "IMC Education and Plymouth Marjon University launch BSc in Applied Psychology in Sri Lanka\n\nIMC Education, in partnership with Plymouth Marjon University, United Kingdom, has officially launched the BSc (Hons) in Applied Psychology programme in Sri Lanka, marking a significant expansion of internationally recognised psychological education in the country.\n\nThe launch event featured a panel discussion on Teenage Mental Health & Psychological First Aid, addressing one of Sri Lanka\u2019s most pressing public health challenges. Distinguished speakers included Dr. Amila B. Kulathunga (CEO, IMC Education), Prof. Inoka C. Perera (Director of Academics), and Dr. Katheryn Edwards from Plymouth Marjon University, alongside other academic and clinical professionals.\n\nThe programme follows British Psychological Society (BPS)-accredited curriculum standards, providing students with a rigorous academic foundation and practical competencies for careers in clinical, educational, counselling, and community psychology settings.\n\nAI Catalyst Symposium 2026 urges shift from ambition to execution\n\nUS-Iran peace accord lifts CSE sentiment; turnover hits Rs 3.1bn\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
