    "md5": "cb9b5c79ec2f1e28dd9627278846f801",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1751,
    "chunk_text": "25 Thai delegates to attend SL-Thailand Business Council silver jubilee celebrations\n\nThailand\u2019s Board of Trade to be represented by 25-member strong business delegation\n\nToday marks a significant milestone in the history of Sri Lanka\u2013-Thailand economic relations as the Sri Lanka-Thailand Business Council (SLTBC) celebrates its silver jubilee, commemorating 25 years of fostering trade, investment, business collaboration and enduring friendship between the two nations.\n\nThe prestigious celebration will take place this evening at The Kingsbury Hotel, Colombo, bringing together an influential gathering of business leaders, diplomats, policymakers, entrepreneurs and stakeholders from both countries to honour a remarkable journey that has helped shape one of the region\u2019s most dynamic bilateral business partnerships.\n\nAdding further significance to the occasion, the event will welcome a distinguished 25-member business delegation from Thailand\u2019s Board of Trade, reaffirming the growing strength and strategic importance of economic ties between Sri Lanka and Thailand.\n\nThe SLTBC was founded with a bold vision to transform the longstanding cultural and historical ties between Sri Lanka and Thailand into a thriving economic partnership. Over the past 25 years, the SLTBC has emerged as a catalyst for bilateral trade, investment and business growth, creating invaluable opportunities for enterprises to connect, collaborate and expand beyond borders.\n\nThrough influential business forums, high-level trade missions, strategic partnerships and impactful networking platforms, the SLTBC has played a pivotal role in strengthening commercial relations while fostering innovation, knowledge exchange and sustainable economic development."
  },
