    "md5": "6faa73a0d29cce8e77792ba9869a1bff",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1090,
    "chunk_text": "The launch was graced by the senior officials from the Foreign Affairs Ministry and representatives of the SLBFE. International partners, including the UN\u2019s International Labour Organisation, which supported the initiative as a Technical Partner, were also present.\n\nIn 2025, Sri Lankan overseas workers contributed a record US $ 8.07 billion in remittances to the national economy, highlighting the vital role they play in sustaining families, strengthening communities and powering the country\u2019s development. The app is designed to honour their contributions and keep them connected to their motherland, wherever they may be.\n\nThrough the Lankakonect app, SLT\u2011Mobitel has reaffirmed its commitment to the government\u2019s vision of a fully digitised Sri Lanka where technology signifies progress in service of the people.\n\nThe launch at the Foreign Affairs Ministry signals Sri Lanka\u2019s broader push to bring overseas mission services online, strengthening ties between embassies and expatriate communities and reinforcing national identity and belonging for every Sri Lankan abroad."
