    "md5": "2e5446bde9f22a69eb43f9ecc9e83d3c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 960,
    "chunk_text": "President\u2019s Fund provides laptops to 14 university students\n\nColombo, June 19 (Daily Mirror) - The President\u2019s Fund yesterday provided laptop computers to 14 university students selected from applications submitted through Divisional Secretariat offices across the country.\n\nThe distribution programme was held at the Head Office of the President\u2019s Fund, with Rs. 5.8 million allocated for the initiative.\n\nAccording to the President\u2019s Media Division (PMD), the programme is aimed at supporting university students by providing essential educational equipment.\n\nThe PMD said that nearly 30 university students have received educational equipment through the President\u2019s Fund during 2025 and 2026, with more than Rs. 9.8 million spent on the programme so far.\n\nSecretary to the President\u2019s Fund and Senior Additional Secretary to the President Roshan Gamage, senior officials of the President\u2019s Fund, parents and other invitees attended the event."
