    "chunk_size_bytes": 1336,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka promotes Colombo Port City as investment destination in Oman\n\nThe Embassy of Sri Lanka in Oman, together with the Colombo Port City Commission and CHEC Port City, organised a roadshow in Muscat to promote Colombo Port City as a key investment destination.\n\nSpeaking at the event held at Sheraton Hotel in Muscat, Sri Lanka\u2019s Ambassador to Oman W.A.K.S. De Alwis invited the Omani investors to explore opportunities in Colombo Port City, highlighting Sri Lanka\u2019s strategic location connecting the Gulf region with South Asia.\n\nThe ambassador also noted that the Colombo Port City Commission serves as a single-window investment facilitator, making it easier for the investors to do business within the special economic zone.\n\nThe event was attended by senior Omani government officials, including Under Secretary of State for Investment Ibtisam bint Al Farooji and Under Secretary of State for Tourism and Heritage Azzan bin Qassim Al Busaidi, along with leading Omani business leaders and private sector representatives.\n\nDuring the visit, the Sri Lankan delegation, led by Colombo Port City Commission Chairman Harsha Amarasekera, also held discussions with the senior officials of the Oman Investment Authority and Oman Public Authority for Special Economic Zones to strengthen investment ties between the two countries."
