    "chunk_size_bytes": 1515,
    "chunk_text": "The digital declaration from the summit revealed another battlefield. The G7\u2019s proposals on protecting children online, artificial intelligence safety and algorithm transparency appear focused on social responsibility, but they also represent a struggle over control of the digital environment.\n\nThe reactions from Moscow and Pyongyang demonstrated how limited Western influence has become. Russian officials claimed European leaders had influenced Trump\u2019s thinking at the summit while carefully avoiding a direct confrontation with the American president. North Korea rejected the G7\u2019s call for denuclearisation, repeating that its nuclear arsenal was an irreversible security requirement.\n\nThe most revealing image from this year\u2019s summit was not a speech, a handshake or a formal declaration. It was a room full of leaders adjusting their schedules around one individual because they understood the cost of conflict was greater than the embarrassment of waiting.\n\nThat is the new reality of the G7. The club still has influence, but it no longer owns the room. It now has to negotiate with those inside it, those outside it and the changing world that no longer accepts that a small group of nations can decide everything.\n\n\u201cOne more such victory and we are done for\u201d \u2013 King Pyrrhus of Epirus, in 279 B.C.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
