    "chunk_size_bytes": 1956,
    "chunk_text": "He is the only politician that was emotionally committed to bring some economic prosperity to rural Sri Lanka. His intention was to create employment opportunities in the rural areas by bringing industry to the rural countryside. Sadly he was killed and we did not get a picture of the full scenario he had in mind. His vision (we guess) was perhaps to create prosperous villages, and help the poor to be less poor. It was probably very different from a vision of using the rural poor to provide cheap labour for industry..\n\nIt was Marx and Lenin who said that then existing economic mould that had created the economic scenario prevailing at that time in Russia had to be completely destroyed and replaced with one that will create an egalitarian society. We too need a radically different economic mould that will ensure that funds and other resources flow into economic activities that will make poor less poor..\n\nCreate a raft of prosperous villages, building around the traditional activities in that area.\n\nIf there is fishing then create a vibrant fishing industry.Provide cold storage facilites for every group of fishing villages. Provide cold storage vehicles for transporting fish to other parts of the country. Ensure that all the other facilities required like rescue boats are provided. This will create clusters of prosperous villages around the country. If there are spices then create prosperous village around spices\n\nProvide what is required to sustain these villages \u2013 good roads, access to medical\n\nThe new mould should facilitate the flow of resources to activities that will reduce poverty The State should provide all of this as a part of their economic plans for the country. There is need to be ruthless. If there is a foreign exchange cost, and if this could be found only by stopping the imports of cars, this should be done until adequate funds are available.\n\nRevitalizing villages could also be a route to generate exports."
