    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka and Russia forge path to enhanced tourism ties at Moscow Forum\n\nThe 6th Let\u2019s Travel International Tourism Forum in Moscow has emerged as a watershed moment for Sri Lanka\u2019s tourism diplomacy, with high-level discussions on direct flights, simplified visas, and regional market expansion taking centre stage.\n\nDeputy Minister of Tourism Prof. Ruwan Ranasinghe led the Sri Lankan delegation in pivotal meetings with Russian Deputy Minister of Economic Development Dmitry Vakhrukov, where discussions on destination promotion, familiarisation tours, and improved air connectivity addressed critical logistical barriers to increasing tourist arrivals.\n\nSpeaking at two high-level panel sessions on \u201cDirect flights, simplified visas and what this means for the industry\u201d and \u201cTourism of national importance: The strategic potential of international cooperation,\u201d the Deputy Minister emphasised Sri Lanka\u2019s commitment to facilitating seamless travel and building enduring partnerships. His comments underscored Sri Lanka\u2019s strategic push to become a more accessible year-round destination for Russian travellers.\n\nCEAT opens premium Shop-in-Shop outlet at Olympic Tyre House, Colombo 6\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s enterprise leaders chart course for secure AI adoption at Innovation Forum 2026\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
