    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "f991a470e6c87da16b7dd450a13ca7a1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1644,
    "chunk_text": "FitsAir launches exclusive direct service between Colombo and Ahmedabad\n\nFrom left: Shafiya Careem, Head of Marketing and Communications, FitsAir; Najath Suruba, Acting Chief Commercial Officer, FitsAir; K. Munasinghe, Senior Vice President, Cinnamon Hotels &amp; Resorts; Nalaka Amaratunga, Senior Vice President, John Keells Holdings PLC; Victoria Fuh, Head of Commercial, Cinnamon Hotels &amp; Resorts; Anupama Ranasinghe, Manager Marketing, Cinnamon Life at City of Dreams and Ammar Kassim, Executive Director, FitsAir.\n\nFitsAir officially commenced direct operations between Colombo and Ahmedabad on June 19, 2026, becoming the only airline to offer non-stop flights between the two cities.\n\nOperating three times weekly, the new service strengthens connectivity between Sri Lanka and Western India while offering greater convenience for both leisure and business travellers. Ahmedabad, one of India\u2019s leading commercial centres and the gateway to Gujarat, represents a key market for tourism, trade, and investment.\n\nThe inaugural flight marks another milestone in FitsAir\u2019s network expansion strategy. As Sri Lanka\u2019s first privately-owned airline, this reinforces its commitment to enhancing regional connectivity through affordable travel. A special launch ceremony was held to commemorate the occasion, attended by representatives from FitsAir, the travel trade, tourism sector, Walker\u2019s Tours, Cinnamon Hotels & Resorts, and Cinnamon Life City of Dreams.\n\nSpeaking at the launch, FitsAir Executive Director Ammar Kassim highlighted that routes transcend airports by connecting dreams, driving trade, and building partnerships."
  },
