    "md5": "1b7a40f7d771a3f4b267b5bc3fa1147b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1062,
    "chunk_text": "Beware of fake PHIs extorting money\n\nColombo, June 22 (Daily Mirror) - The Sri Lanka Public Health Inspectors\u2019 Union has warned the public to be alert to individuals impersonating Public Health Inspectors (PHIs) and extorting money from households and institutions under the guise of official duties.\n\nIn a statement, the Union said several incidents have been reported from different parts of the country where impostors had deceived residents and business establishments by demanding payments while claiming to carry out health inspections.\n\nAccording to the Union, the fraudulent activities are mainly linked to house inspections being conducted during the ongoing dengue outbreak, with scammers exploiting the situation to solicit money.\n\nThe Union stressed that Public Health Inspectors do not charge or collect money under any circumstances in the course of performing their duties.\n\nThe public has therefore been urged not to hand over money to anyone claiming to be a PHI and to immediately report such incidents to the Police and relevant authorities."
  },
