    "chunk_text": "FIFA World Cup 2026 Round of 32 Bracket and Schedule: Road to the Final Takes Shape\n\nJune 23 (Daily Mirror) - The 2026 World Cup is the first in history to send 48 nations into the competition, and that single change has reshaped everything about how teams reach the knockout stage. Where every tournament since 1998 jumped straight from the group stage into a round of 16, this edition adds an entirely new round underneath it: the round of 32. It is the moment the competition stops being about points on a table and becomes pure knockout football, where one bad night ends a country's World Cup outright.\n\nSri Lankan fans following this tournament will want to understand this round properly, because it works differently from any World Cup that has come before it. Here is exactly how the round of 32 is built, who qualifies for it, how the bracket locks into place, and what the schedule looks like all the way through to the final at MetLife Stadium.\n\nThe round of 32 runs from 28 June through 4 July, with all sixteen matches spread across stadiums in the United States, Canada and Mexico. Below is the official match-by-match framework. Team names will replace the placeholders as each spot is confirmed.\n\nGroup-stage draws are allowed and even common. Knockout football does not give that luxury. If a round-of-32 match is level after 90 minutes, the game goes into extra time, played as two 15-minute halves for a total of 30 additional minutes. If the scoreline is still tied after that, the match is decided by a penalty shootout. This format applies through every knockout round, including the final, so a World Cup winner could theoretically be crowned on penalties at MetLife Stadium come 19 July."
  },
