    "chunk_text": "At least 18 dead in France, including two children in hot car, as Europe bakes\n\nReuters - At least 18 people died in France, including two children left in a hot car, as a \u200bheatwave hung over Europe, smashing temperature records in several cities on Monday.\n\nAs schools in France closed or modified timetables, forecasters in Britain predicted temperatures could \u200cbreak records for June this week.\n\nThe temperature in Bordeaux in France's western wine country rose to 41.9 degrees Celsius (107.4 degrees Fahrenheit), breaking a record set last August. In Poitiers in central France it reached 41.2 C, beating a previous high set in 1947.\n\nIn San Sebastian, in Spain's traditionally cooler north, the temperature was set to reach 40 C, more than double the city's historic average for June 22 \u200baccording to the Reuters Climate Monitor, which showed Europe as the continent furthest from its historic norm on Monday.\n\nAn April report by the World Meteorological Organization found \u200bEurope is warming at more than double the global rate."
