    "md5": "6b97cc1a2bf848e6e5be2b32531016dd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1506,
    "chunk_text": "Applications for GIT examination 2026 open until July 16\n\nColombo, June 23 (Daily Mirror) - The Examinations Department has called for applications for the General Information Technology (GIT) Examination 2026, which will be conducted for Grade 12 students in government and private schools.\n\nAccording to the Department, applications will be accepted online from June 22 to July 16, 2026. Only students studying in Grade 12 in 2026 and who are expected to sit the G.C.E. Advanced Level Examination for the first time in 2027 are eligible to apply.\n\nThe Department said all applications must be submitted through the respective principals or heads of schools. School authorities have been instructed to access the Department\u2019s official websites and submit applications online after following the relevant guidelines. Individual candidates will not be allowed to submit applications on their own.\n\nApplicants are required to use the usernames and passwords already issued to government and private school principals. A printed copy of the submitted application should be retained for future reference.\n\nThe Department further said that, in the case of private school candidates, examination fees must be paid only after all student details have been entered into the database, adding that no re-admissions or amendments will be permitted after payment.\n\nFor further information, applicants may contact the Department through its hotline 1911 or via telephone numbers 0112784537, 0112786616 and 0112784208."
