    "date_str": "2026-06-23",
    "description": "Regen Renewables hands over 45.63 kW rooftop solar PV system to CEB\u2019s NSCC",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.dailymirror.lk/business-news/Regen-Renewables-hands-over-45-63-kW-rooftop-solar-PV-system-to-CEBs-NSCC/273-343720",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "dailymirrorlk",
    "time_ut": 1782238486.0,
    "chunk_id": "2026-06-23-dailymirrorlk-e6881b74-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "da45006ce5f2e1d6b8f9fd2e99c18eb9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1816,
    "chunk_text": "Regen Renewables hands over 45.63 kW rooftop solar PV system to CEB\u2019s NSCC\n\nRegen Renewables Chief Technology Officer Champika Periyapperuma and\u00a0 National System Control Centre Director Buddhika Samarasekara at official handover ceremony\n\nRegen Renewables (Pvt.) Ltd recently marked another milestone in Sri Lanka\u2019s renewable energy journey, with the successful completion and official handover of a 45.63 kW rooftop solar PV system to the former Ceylon Electricity Board (CEB) at the National System Control Centre (NSCC) now known as National Operation Centre (NOC), located at No. 80, Parliament Road, Pelawatte, Battaramulla.\n\nThe project, which was awarded to Regen Renewables through a competitive tender process, was completed on schedule and within budget, reinforcing the company\u2019s reputation for delivering high-quality renewable energy solutions to both public and private sector clients.\n\nThe official handover ceremony was conducted by Regen Renewables Chief Technology Officer Eng. Champika Periyapperuma to System Control Centre Director Eng. Buddhika Samarasekara, symbolising the strong institutional partnership between the two organisations.\n\nThe rooftop solar installation forms part of the CEB\u2019s broader initiative to integrate renewable energy into its operational infrastructure while strengthening the sustainability of Sri Lanka\u2019s national power system. Designed and engineered to ensure reliable performance and long-term energy generation, it also provides an important operational advantage for the NOC.\n\nSpeaking on the importance of the roof top solar system at the NOC office, Engineer Samarasekara commented that the system provides a mechanism for forecasting and validation of roof top solar generation in order to provide a better service to the consumers and investors."
  },
