    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "b24a86e0fa8fa8840efbde4a1afc7aff",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1409,
    "chunk_text": "Speaking on the importance of the roof top solar system at the NOC office, Engineer Samarasekara commented that the system provides a mechanism for forecasting and validation of roof top solar generation in order to provide a better service to the consumers and investors.\n\nThe project further builds on Regen Renewables\u2019 successful collaboration with the CEB, following the completion of a 60-kW rooftop solar PV system at the CEB head office building in 2023. Together, these projects highlight the growing role of solar energy within the key operational facilities of Sri Lanka\u2019s national utility provider.\n\nRegen Renewables Managing Director Dr. Lakmal Fernando stated, \u201cThis project represents more than just another solar installation. It reflects the growing momentum towards renewable energy integration in Sri Lanka and the importance of partnerships between the private sector and national institutions. We are proud to support the CEB in advancing sustainable energy solutions while contributing to the country\u2019s long-term energy security.\n\nEng. Periyapperuma, added, \u201cOur engineering team worked closely with the CEB engineers to ensure that the system meets the highest technical standards. The project demonstrates the strength of local engineering expertise and our ability to deliver complex public-sector renewable energy projects with precision, reliability and professionalism.\u201d"
  },
