    "language": "en",
    "md5": "805de8f0f914420d469aa0406e64a482",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1988,
    "chunk_text": "D P Logistics renamed as David Pieris Logistics\n\nRegional expansion plans into Asian and Middle Eastern markets underway\n\nDavid Pieris Group announced that D P Logistics (Private) Limited has officially changed its name to David Pieris Logistics (Private) Limited (DPL), marking a significant milestone in the company\u2019s continued growth and integration within the group\u2019s expanding logistics portfolio.\n\nThe name change reflects the company\u2019s strengthened identity under the David Pieris group brand and its enhanced position as a leading end-to-end logistics and supply chain solutions provider in Sri Lanka and overseas.\n\nDPL currently ranks amongst the top 10 companies in warehousing and third-party logistics (3PL) operations in the country and manages one of the largest container fleets within the local logistics sector.\n\nDespite operating in a highly fragmented freight forwarding market, the company continues to grow its market share, reinforcing its reputation as one of the few local logistics providers with comprehensive expertise across all logistics disciplines.\n\nIn line with its expansion strategy, the David Pieris group acquired Pulsar Shipping Agencies (Pvt.) Limited, formerly the shipping arm of Expolanka Holdings PLC, in 2022. This acquisition enabled the group to strengthen its logistics and shipping cluster by expanding into ship agency services, husbandry services and marine logistics, further broadening its service capabilities.\n\nThrough these strategic integrations, DPL now offers a fully comprehensive portfolio of services, including container transportation, distribution and project logistics, freight forwarding, customs clearance, 3PL, warehousing and supply chain management.\n\nFurther strengthening its international footprint, the David Pieris group has also acquired a 50 percent stake in Navire Logistics Services L.L.C, a reputed logistics company based in Dubai and its fully-owned subsidiary in Muscat and Salalah, Sultanate of Oman."
  },
