    "chunk_size_bytes": 1236,
    "chunk_text": "Ronaldo becomes first player to score at six World Cups as Portugal thrash Uzbekistan\n\nHouston, June 24 (Daily Mirror) - Cristiano Ronaldo etched his name further into football history as Portugal cruised to a 5-0 victory over Uzbekistan in their Group K clash in Houston.\n\nThe Portuguese captain became the first player to score in six FIFA World Cups when he opened the scoring early in the match, ending a 10-game goal drought at major international tournaments. Ronaldo converted from close range after a pinpoint cross from Joao Cancelo, netting his 144th international goal in his record-extending 230th appearance for Portugal.\n\nRonaldo added a second before halftime, moving closer to early Golden Boot leader Lionel Messi. The brace also saw him equal Eusebio\u2019s Portuguese World Cup scoring record of nine goals. Nuno Mendes and Rafael Leao got on the scoresheet, while an own goal by Abdukodir Khusanov completed the rout as Portugal bounced back emphatically from their 1-1 draw against DR Congo.\n\nWhat Do Sri Lankan Fans Think? Ranking the Top Contenders for the FIFA World Cup 2026\n\nFIFA World Cup 2026: 10 Best Group Stage Matches to Watch in Sri Lanka\n\nFIFA World Cup 2026 Results: Every Match from Group Stage to Final"
  },
