    "md5": "0c64d6dbc6314f2862cf3d780964fe0a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1713,
    "chunk_text": "Sarvodaya Development Finance records strong FY2025/26 performance\n\nSarvodaya Development Finance PLC (SDF) has delivered a strong financial performance for the year ended 31 March 2026, recording significant growth in income, profitability, portfolio expansion, and asset quality while continuing its commitment to responsible and inclusive finance.\n\nFor the financial year under review, SDF reported total income of Rs. 6.42 billion, a year-on year increase of 46.8 percent. Interest income rose by 43.8 percent to Rs. 5.85 billion, driven by business expansion and growth in earning assets.\n\nNet Interest Income increased by 35.4 percent to Rs. 3.58\u00a0 billion, while Total Operating Income grew by 40.8 percent to Rs. 4.15 billion, reflecting the\u00a0 Company\u2019s ability to generate strong and sustainable earnings.\n\nProfitability improved substantially during the year. Operating Profit before Tax on Financial\u00a0 Services increased by 59.9 percent to Rs. 1.82 billion, while Profit Before Tax rose by 63.8 percent to Rs.1.36 billion.\n\nProfit for the Year increased by 73.1 percent to Rs. 820.1 million compared with Rs. 473.8 million in the previous year. Earnings per share improved to Rs. 5.48, demonstrating enhanced value creation for shareholders.\n\nThe Company\u2019s balance sheet expanded significantly, with total assets increasing by 65.8 percent to Rs. 37.37 billion as at 31 March 2026. Financial assets at amortized cost, including loans and receivables, grew by 67.2 percent to Rs. 20.60 billion, while lease rental receivables increased by 34.0 percent to Rs. 9.19 billion. SDF also strengthened its funding profile through debt securities, including Sustainable Bonds, amounting to Rs. 2.09 billion."
