    "chunk_text": "The Company\u2019s balance sheet expanded significantly, with total assets increasing by 65.8 percent to Rs. 37.37 billion as at 31 March 2026. Financial assets at amortized cost, including loans and receivables, grew by 67.2 percent to Rs. 20.60 billion, while lease rental receivables increased by 34.0 percent to Rs. 9.19 billion. SDF also strengthened its funding profile through debt securities, including Sustainable Bonds, amounting to Rs. 2.09 billion.\n\nSDF maintained a strong capital position, with a Tier 1 Capital Adequacy Ratio of 15.48 percent and a Total Capital Adequacy Ratio of 22.13 percent, both comfortably above regulatory requirements. Asset quality also improved, with the Gross Stage 3 Loans Ratio declining to 4.93 percent from 7.88 percent and the\u00a0 Net Stage 3 Loans Ratio improving to 2.94 percent from 5.70 percent. The Stage 3 Impairment Coverage Ratio strengthened to 42.60 percent.\n\nOperational efficiency improved as the Cost-to-Income Ratio reduced to 42.99 percent, while Return on\u00a0 Equity increased to 19.60 percent. Reflecting its stronger financial position, SDF\u2019s external credit rating was upgraded to Lanka Ratings (SL) BBB- Stable."
