    "chunk_size_bytes": 1714,
    "chunk_text": "Teldeniya car death suspect arrested; Trail of multi-million rupee scams exposed\n\nColombo, June 25 (Daily Mirror) - A series of financial frauds has been uncovered following the arrest of a suspect wanted in connection with the death of a woman found inside a car in Teldeniya.\n\nPolice have arrested the 43-year-old main suspect, along with his wife and a young child, during a joint operation in Jaffna yesterday.\n\nNuwara Eliya Headquarters Police, along with special police teams, have launched a manhunt for a suspect after a 33-year-old physiotherapist's body was found inside a car parked near the Teldeniya Hospital last week.\n\nThe suspect was accused of posing as a software engineer and transporting the body of the physiotherapist from Nuwara Eliya to Kandy and Teldeniya. The victim has been identified as Rathnayake Pathiranage Shyama Darshani, a physiotherapist attached to the Ampara Hospital.\n\nThe investigation began on June 17, 2026, when the body of the victim, a resident of Weligama, was discovered inside a car near the Teldeniya Hospital. While the Teldeniya Police initially responded to the scene, further investigations were handed over to the Nuwara Eliya Police after it was revealed that the events leading to the crime had transpired within the Nuwara Eliya police jurisdiction.\n\nActing on intelligence, a team of officers from the Walana Central Anti-Vice Striking Unit tracked the victim's boyfriend and his 35-year-old wife, both residents of Pallekele, to the Jaffna area, where they were arrested in the early hours of June 24.\n\nFollowing their arrest by the Walana Central Anti-Vice Striking Unit, initial investigations have exposed the male suspect's extensive criminal history."
