    "md5": "a47cebc2e5ac1a7b59d1e16c2725cd8c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1886,
    "chunk_text": "Acting on intelligence, a team of officers from the Walana Central Anti-Vice Striking Unit tracked the victim's boyfriend and his 35-year-old wife, both residents of Pallekele, to the Jaffna area, where they were arrested in the early hours of June 24.\n\nFollowing their arrest by the Walana Central Anti-Vice Striking Unit, initial investigations have exposed the male suspect's extensive criminal history.\n\nFurther investigations uncovered a massive trail of financial fraud. Among his pending court cases is a lawsuit in the Gampaha Magistrate's Court, where he is accused of defrauding a victim of over Rs 11.8 million under the pretext of marriage, alongside charges of illegal vehicle usage. He faces two additional cases at the Aluthkade Magistrate's Court No. 05 for defrauding two other individuals of Rs 1.7 million and Rs 1.3 million using the same matrimonial ruse.\n\nBeyond marriage scams, the suspect's fraudulent activities extended to vehicular and overseas employment rackets.\n\nPolice said he is facing a trial at the Tissamaharama Magistrate's Court for swindling Rs. 2.2 million by promising to import vehicles from foreign countries, as well as an Aluthkade Magistrate's Court case for a Rs 4,200,000 foreign employment scam.\n\nIn addition, the Criminal Investigation Department (CID) has filed four other pending cases against him across the Aluthkade, Horana, and Kaduwela Magistrate Courts.\n\nMeanwhile, a driver from the Kundasale Pradeshiya Sabha was also arrested for aiding and abetting the main suspect in connection with the incident.\n\nPolice said that a special police team from the Nuwara Eliya Police went to the Kundasale area and arrested the individual yesterday (24).\n\nInvestigations revealed that the main suspect involved in the death of the woman is a friend of the suspect driver, and the driver was arrested based on the suspect's phone record data."
