    "md5": "fb27d5d34514a82fe2483a425fb80029",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1890,
    "chunk_text": "Redington-IBM host Innovation Forum Sri Lanka 2026\n\nBring together Sri Lanka\u2019s enterprise leaders to accelerate AI-driven transformation\n\nFlagship forum highlights role of secure AI, ecosystem collaboration and enterprise innovation in advancing Sri Lanka\u2019s digital economy\n\nRedington, in collaboration with IBM, successfully hosted IBM Innovation Forum Sri Lanka 2026 recently, at Cinnamon Life City of Dreams, bringing together senior business leaders, technology decision-makers, government representatives and ecosystem partners to discuss the future of secure, AI-driven enterprise transformation.\n\nHeld under the theme \u2018Building Secure, AI-Driven and Autonomous Enterprises in Sri Lanka\u2019, the forum provided a platform for organisations to explore how emerging technologies can accelerate innovation, strengthen resilience and deliver measurable business outcomes.\n\nCommenting on the significance of the forum, Redington CEO ASEAN and South Asia Cem Borhan said, \u201cSri Lanka is entering a defining phase in its digital transformation journey. Organisations are increasingly focused on converting technology investments into measurable business outcomes. Through the IBM Innovation Forum, we are bringing together leaders from across government, industry and technology to exchange insights and enable practical pathways for AI-driven transformation. Our collaboration with IBM reflects a shared commitment to helping enterprises innovate responsibly, strengthen resilience and unlock long-term growth.\u201d\n\nAligned with Sri Lanka\u2019s National Digital Economy Strategy 2030, the forum featured discussions on enterprise AI adoption, cybersecurity, infrastructure modernisation, data protection, operational resilience and governance. Industry experts shared practical perspectives on how organisations can move beyond experimentation to operationalise AI securely and at scale."
  },
