    "chunk_text": "The event drew participation from state-sector authorities, research institutions, academia, engineering students and public and private sector organisations, creating a dynamic platform for engagement across the construction industry.\n\nA key feature of the summit was a high-level panel discussion on \u2018Building a Resilient and Sustainable Construction Future\u2019, featuring several distinguished industry leaders.\n\nSenior Professor Priyan Mendis from University of Melbourne speaks at Build Beyond 2026 Summit\n\nProf. Bishnoi delivered two keynote presentations on low-carbon construction technologies. His first session \u2018Development and Use of Low Carbon Cements\u2019, explored his work on Limestone Calcined Clay Cement (LC3) and the development of the LC3 standard adopted by the Bureau of Indian Standards. His second presentation \u2018Design and Application of Low Carbon Concretes\u2019 addressed sustainable concrete solutions in relation to the Sri Lankan construction sector.\n\nProf. Mendis delivered his keynote on \u2018Net Zero: Materials to Novel Structural Applications\u2019. He highlighted the role of high-performance concrete in improving durability, strength and resistance to environmental stress in modern high-rise and large-scale structures. Drawing from international case studies and his experience in serving several Australian and international standards committees related to concrete structures and structural loading, Prof. Mendis shared insights from his involvement in the construction of iconic projects including Burj Khalifa, Merdeka 118, Eureka Tower and Lotus Tower.\n\nRepresenting the Tokyo Cement group, Director R&D Dr. M.G.M.U. Ismail and Director Innovations Praveen Gnanam presented the company\u2019s latest advancements in cement and concrete technologies, reinforcing its focus on sustainable and innovative construction solutions."
