    "chunk_size_bytes": 1440,
    "chunk_text": "Entrepreneurship for a greener future: Tackling environmental challenges and sustainability\n\nSustainable entrepreneurship helps generate innovative solutions to address these environmental challenges while promoting economic and social development\n\nSustainability, environmental issues, and entrepreneurship are significant factors in today's world.\n\nSustainability is the ability to meet current needs without limiting the ability of future generations to meet their own needs. Environmental issues include pollution, climate change, deforestation, excessive waste generation, and biodiversity loss. All these issues affect communities and the entire globe. Due to rapid industrialisation, urbanisation, and population growth, increasing pressure is being placed on the environment. This is why the relationship between sustainability and entrepreneurship is significant, as business activities can have negative impacts on the environment.\n\nCurrently, various environmental challenges are pushing the world towards unsustainable development. Climate change is among the most serious problems, resulting from greenhouse gas emissions generated by various industrial and production processes. For instance, the increasing occurrence of natural disasters, including floods, droughts, and heat waves across the globe, highlights the severity of climate change. The recent Cyclone Ditwah that affected Sri Lanka was a result of climate change."
