    "chunk_size_bytes": 1162,
    "chunk_text": "Currently, various environmental challenges are pushing the world towards unsustainable development. Climate change is among the most serious problems, resulting from greenhouse gas emissions generated by various industrial and production processes. For instance, the increasing occurrence of natural disasters, including floods, droughts, and heat waves across the globe, highlights the severity of climate change. The recent Cyclone Ditwah that affected Sri Lanka was a result of climate change.\n\nEntrepreneurs play a very important role in tackling these problems through the practice of sustainable entrepreneurship. When entrepreneurs engage in sustainable entrepreneurship, they focus on identifying ecological problems as business opportunities. Moreover, they generate innovations that reduce environmental problems while creating profits. For instance, entrepreneurs in the renewable energy sector are working to provide solar, wind, and hydro energy solutions to reduce dependence on fossil fuels. Similarly, companies such as Tesla have revolutionised the electric vehicle industry, helping to reduce the environmental impact of conventional vehicles."
