    "chunk_size_bytes": 1932,
    "chunk_text": "Exterminators launches MACCP X mosquito intelligence platform\n\nExterminators PLC and Sentario UK Ltd. announced the launch of the MACCP X Mosquito Intelligence Platform, an AI-powered system developed to advance disease surveillance, environmental intelligence, risk mapping, and predictive mosquito management across Sri Lanka.\n\nDeveloped by Exterminators PLC and Sentario UK Ltd., Founder and Managing Director Denham Marlon Ferreira, the platform builds on the MACCP 2000 (Mosquito Analysis Critical Control Points) framework introduced in 2018. MACCP X integrates artificial intelligence, predictive analytics, environmental monitoring, geographic intelligence, and disease surveillance to help identify mosquito and disease risks earlier.\n\nCovering all provinces and districts of Sri Lanka under an AI for Social Good initiative, MACCP Xmarks the first phase of an AI-enabled mosquito early warning ecosystem. It is designed to support public health authorities, organisations, communities, and mosquito management professionals with data-driven insights and predictive intelligence. Solutions include Disease surveillance and environmental monitoring; Geographic intelligence and risk mapping; Predictive analytics for earlier intervention and Decision support for targeted mosquito management.\n\nAccording to the World Health Organisation (WHO), mosquito-borne diseases affect more than 700 million people each year and cause over 700,000 deaths worldwide. Climate change, urbanisation, population growth, and shifting weather patterns are increasing mosquito-related disease risks, highlighting the need for more proactive prevention strategies.\n\n\u201cPrevention delivers greater value than reaction,\u201d said Denham Marlon Ferreira. \u201cMACCP X combines field expertise with artificial intelligence to identify risks earlier, strengthen decision-making, and support the protection of people, communities, and the environment.\u201d"
