    "md5": "fe323a8ce1f3bdc6ebd88c1c3c70af11",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1632,
    "chunk_text": "Investment Forum in Toronto highlights opportunities in Sri Lanka for Canadian investors\n\nThe Consulate General of Sri Lanka in Toronto and the Board of Investment (BOI) of Sri Lanka conducted a virtual forum on Investment Opportunities in Sri Lanka on 18 June 2026, attended by approximately 40 members of the Sri Lankan diaspora and prospective investors in Canada.\n\nOpening the event, Consul General Medhavi Peiris noted that the forum was organised in response to the increasing number of inquiries received from interested individuals, diaspora community regarding investing in Sri Lanka. She stated that the objective was to provide updated information on investment opportunities in Sri Lanka, address misconceptions, and facilitate direct engagement with relevant institutions.\n\nAddressing the forum, Foreign Affairs Ministry Economic Affairs Bilateral Division Director General Manori Mallikaratchy, highlighted the importance of strengthening investment ties with the Sri Lankan diaspora and encouraged participants to explore opportunities in Sri Lanka. She also promoted Sri Lanka Expo 2027 as a key platform for investors and businesses.\n\nBOI Director General Renuka Weerakone emphasised the importance of continued engagement with diaspora investors and reaffirmed the BOI\u2019s commitment to supporting and facilitating investments.\n\nPresentations by BOI Executive Director Priyanka Samaraweera, and Director - Investment Promotion, Ganga Palaketiya provided participants with an overview of investment opportunities across key sectors, structured projects, and updated information on incentives available to investors."
