    "chunk_text": "Three-decade journey: BOI Director General Renuka Weerakone bids farewell\n\nThis week marked the close of a remarkable chapter in Sri Lanka\u2019s investment promotion history, as Board of Investment of Sri Lanka (BOI) Director General Renuka M. Weerakone relinquishes her position on 25 June after more than three decades of unbroken service to the institution she has helped shape and steer.\n\nWeerakone joined the BOI on 1 June 1994 as an Assistant Manager (Legal), beginning a career that would see her rise, step by deliberate step, through nearly every tier of the organisation, from Assistant Manager, Senior Manager, Acting Director, Director, Executive Director, Acting Director General, and finally Director General. Few public-sector careers trace so complete an arc within a single institution, and fewer still touch as many of its functions along the way. Over the years, she served in the Regional Development Department, the Project Implementation Department, the Regional Development and Special Projects Department, the Investment Promotion Department, the Director General\u2019s Secretariat, the Investment Appraisal Department, and the Project Monitoring Department, as well as held the position of secretary to board for the 5 years, a breadth of exposure that gave her an unusually complete view of how investment moves from policy to project on the ground.\n\nBefore the BOI, Weerakone engaged as an Instructing Attorney at a leading Colombo law firm, having qualified as an Attorney-at-Law, Notary Public, and Commissioner for Oaths. She would later add a Master\u2019s Degree in Business Administration from the Postgraduate Institute of Management, University of Sri Jayewardenepura, pairing legal precision with strategic and managerial depth. This combination came to define her approach to institution-building at the BOI."
  },
