    "md5": "f51a0a1b4f70383890f8f5ddeda15290",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1693,
    "chunk_text": "Before the BOI, Weerakone engaged as an Instructing Attorney at a leading Colombo law firm, having qualified as an Attorney-at-Law, Notary Public, and Commissioner for Oaths. She would later add a Master\u2019s Degree in Business Administration from the Postgraduate Institute of Management, University of Sri Jayewardenepura, pairing legal precision with strategic and managerial depth. This combination came to define her approach to institution-building at the BOI.\n\nHer contribution beyond the BOI has been equally significant. She serves as a Board Member of the Export Development Board (EDB) and the International Chamber of Commerce (ICC) Sri Lanka, extending her influence into the broader trade and commerce ecosystem. In 2025, that body of work was recognised when she was awarded the \u201cWomen in Investment and International Trade Leadership\u201d title at the Top50 Professional & Career Women Global Awards, a fitting tribute to a career built on quiet, sustained impact rather than the pursuit of recognition.\n\nHaving stepped away after 32 years of service, Weerakone reflects on the vantage point that retirement affords: \u201cRetirement from a long career in senior public service brings a unique vantage point. It allows one to step away from the daily crises of administration and look at the broader horizon of our national trajectory. Over the span of my career, I have watched our institutions weather economic shifts, political transitions, and unprecedented global challenges. What this journey has taught me is that the strength of a nation does not lie solely in its governmental directives, but in the resilience, continuity, and integrity of its administrative backbone.\u201d"
  },
