    "md5": "182936f579dcc4af0ebbf24e465d070c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1979,
    "chunk_text": "SLIIT Business School\u2019s \u2018SoftSkills+ 2026\u2019 puts country\u2019s future leaders in the spotlight\n\nFrom 112 teams, 48 contenders made it to The Grand Finale of \u2018SoftSkills+ 2026\u2019, organized by the SLIIT Business School.\n\nSLIIT was a hive of energy on 16 May, as 192 students from all districts of Sri Lanka displayed leadership, communication, creativity and teamwork. Vying for first place at the prestigious event, SoftSkills+ served as a vibrant platform to celebrate and encourage talent among the future generation of leaders.\n\nThe event reflected the growing importance of soft skills development among the younger generation and highlighted SLIIT Business School\u2019s commitment to nurturing future-ready leaders.\n\nMethodist College Colombo emerged champions of SoftSkills+ 2026, while Ratnapura Sivali Central College placed as runners up, Badulla Central College claimed the 2nd runner-up title.\n\nThe occasion was graced by Chaaminda Kumarasiri, Chairman of ACCA Sri Lanka, who attended as the Chief Guest. Addressing the gathering, he emphasized the significance of communication, leadership, adaptability, and interpersonal skills in today\u2019s rapidly evolving professional landscape.\n\nArtist Madani Malwattage and Tharindu Weerasinghe Senior Lecturer University of Kelaniya conducted an engaging Soft Skills Development Workshop for the participants. Their insightful sessions inspired students to enhance skills which are essential in today\u2019s professional settings.\n\nSoftSkills+ 2026 was supported by several leading organizations and brands that contributed towards making the event a remarkable success.\n\nThe competition concluded on a highly competitive yet celebratory note, recognizing outstanding performances from schools. Ranitha Weerarathna, Coordinator SoftSkills+2026 and Senior Lecturer-SLIIT Business School stated, \u00abThe remarkable success and positive impact of this year\u2019s event have undoubtedly set a strong foundation for future editions\u201d."
