    "chunk_size_bytes": 1956,
    "chunk_text": "Sheraton Colombo brings flavours of Malaysia with \u2018Spice Trails of Malaysia\u2019\n\nSheraton Colombo Hotel invites guests to embark on an extraordinary culinary journey through Malaysia with \u201cSpice Trails of Malaysia,\u201d an exclusive food festival presented in collaboration with the High Commission of Malaysia in Sri Lanka and Le M\u00e9ridien Kuala Lumpur. Taking place from 26 June to 6 July 2026 at Colombo Kitchen, the festival will be available nightly from 7.00 pm to 10.30 pm.\n\nCelebrating the vibrant multicultural heritage of Malaysia, Spice Trails of Malaysia will showcase the country\u2019s rich tapestry of flavors through an authentic selection of Malay, Chinese and Indian cuisines, alongside beloved street food specialties and regional favorites from Kuala Lumpur, Penang, Melaka and Johor. Guests will have the opportunity to experience the diverse culinary traditions that have established Malaysia as one of Asia\u2019s most celebrated gastronomic destinations.\n\nBringing these authentic flavors to Colombo are two distinguished culinary ambassadors from Le M\u00e9ridien Kuala Lumpur. Leading the showcase is Chef Mohd Khairul Azhar bin Nordin, Sous Chef \u2013 Malay Banquet, whose nearly two decades of culinary expertise have been dedicated to preserving and celebrating Malaysia\u2019s rich food heritage. Having represented Malaysian cuisine internationally and most recently overseen culinary operations for an official royal function at Istana Negara, Chef Azhar is renowned for his mastery of traditional Malay cuisine and banquet gastronomy.\n\nJoining him is Chef Muhammad Fahmi bin Sulaiman, Chef de Partie I, whose culinary journey spans over 15 years across a variety of cuisines including Malay, Indian, Japanese, Western and Italian. Known for his passion for Malaysia\u2019s street food culture and regional specialties, Chef Fahmi brings creativity, technical expertise and a deep appreciation for the flavours that define Malaysian cuisine."
