    "chunk_text": "The event featured public servants, community leaders and civil society representatives from across Sri Lanka, including Chaminda Hettiarachchi of the Department of Pensions, Chameesha De Silva of the Department of Posts, Samali Wathsala Kulathunga of the Grama Niladhari Service, Kithsiri from the Gampaha District Administration, Rubadharshan from the Ministry of Plantation and Community Infrastructure, community representatives Niojini Vinayagam, Anne Subadara Peries and Shiroma Namali, and V. Anthones of the Uva Workers Development Foundation. Through their stories and experiences, they offered unique perspectives on the challenges and opportunities of building more inclusive and connected communities.\n\nSri Lanka is one of many countries participating in the first-ever United Nations Peacebuilding Week, a global initiative marking 20 years since the establishment of the UN Peacebuilding architecture. The week celebrates progress made in supporting countries to prevent conflict and sustain peace, while highlighting the role of dialogue, participation and trust in building more peaceful, inclusive and resilient societies."
