    "md5": "022539800a92e3c6bfb0f419539beffd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1367,
    "chunk_text": "A White Christmas in Nova Scotia\n\nSince leaving Canada I had kept in touch with friends there. One day the phone rang; it was Jim Retson. He invited me to spend Christmas with his family in Truro, north of Halifax in Nova Scotia, a northeastern province of Canada. He had married Roberta and they had a small child.\n\nHalifax is the main city of Nova Scotia. When I arrived at Halifax from Pittsburgh, Jim\u2019s younger sister Mavis met me at the airport. She was very friendly hugging me warmly and invited me to spend the first few days in her apartment in Halifax instead of checking into a hotel. Her companionship was pleasant and she took me sightseeing around Halifax every day. I had the opportunity of seeing giant vessels in the Halifax harbor and we visited the old lighthouse at Peggy\u2019s Cove.\n\nSince Halifax was a small city, I could see most of the important places within a few days. Halifax is famous for its cold water lobster available year-round and we had lobster dinners most nights. The city was covered with several feet of snow and it was indeed a white Christmas and we took part in the celebrations which included sledding and playing ice sports. Mavis\u2019 friends joined us in these activities which were a great delight. We sang Christmas songs, joked, and reminisced about old friends in Toronto, particularly Siva, Surjeet, Liz, and Anette."
