    "chunk_size_bytes": 1803,
    "chunk_text": "Otherwise we can be dissuaded through fear of the way ahead or make wrong choices for robotic activities. We must first question whether robotics is needed for a specific application and then explore what approaches are relevant for the task in hand. Very importantly, we must examine what is in the existing black box and what is already available before implementing new methodology.\n\nThese depend on large amounts of data. But data has many shortcomings such as (1) they concern the past, not present or future; (2) they can be inaccurate, incomplete, or qualitative; (3) they can be qualitative and fuzzy. We should consider other aspects of data, for example \u201cdomain transformation.\u201d Here, it is known that the \u201csource domain\u201d where the data is collected is not typically the same as the \u201caction domain\u201d where the data is applied (used). Other aspects of robots like self-awareness have to be researched as well.\n\nSoftware developments can be accomplished without much capital investment, as is done in India, particularly because many developing countries have highly educated and smart engineers, technicians, and computer scientists. Also, we should focus on advancing the \u201cmechanical capabilities\u201d of robots, which are essential but not just for the local market. Very importantly, we should develop our own guidelines and regulations for robotic ethics and safety which can be done by modifying and enhancing the existing guidelines and regulations in other jurisdictions to suit the local requirements.\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank expands digital banking network with 125th cheque deposit kiosk\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
