    "md5": "87353b5334b4cb919af9b6f281f01f31",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1738,
    "chunk_text": "People\u2019s Bank expands digital banking network with 125th cheque deposit kiosk\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank last week launched its 125th Cheque Deposit Kiosk (CDK), further strengthening its position as a leader in digital banking innovation in Sri Lanka.\n\nThe milestone kiosk was opened at the Self Banking Unit of the bank\u2019s Mid City Branch under the patronage of Chief Executive Officer/General Manager Clive Fonseka. The achievement comes during the bank\u2019s 65th anniversary year and marks the highest number of cheque deposit kiosks deployed by a commercial bank in Sri Lanka to date.\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank introduced its first CDK in July 2021 to coincide with its 60th anniversary, as part of its efforts to provide technology-driven and customer-friendly banking solutions.\n\nThe kiosk facility enables customers to deposit cheques without completing traditional deposit slips. Customers are required to enter only basic details such as their account number, NIC number and telephone number, after which the machine captures cheque images for verification before completing the transaction and issuing an acknowledgement receipt.\n\nThe bank has also introduced an e-receipt facility, allowing customers to receive a secure link via SMS to access details of deposited cheques, including images.\n\nAvailable round the clock at Self Banking Units islandwide, the CDKs allow customers, particularly current account holders, to deposit daily collections after business hours while reducing the need to retain cheques overnight.\n\nPeople\u2019s Bank has also introduced digital endorsement for cheques deposited through CDKs, becoming the first commercial bank in Sri Lanka to implement the feature, which supports a fully digital cheque processing system."
