    "md5": "7f2077017986f612f3702af3b1b4c831",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 919,
    "chunk_text": "The 2027 ICC Olympics Qualifier will feature eight teams in both the men's and women's competitions. Seven places will be filled by the next highest-ranked eligible teams in the respective ICC T20I rankings, excluding those that have already qualified for LA28, with the winner claiming the final Olympic berth.\n\nEach qualified nation will name a 15-player squad. The six teams in each event will be split into two groups of three, with teams playing the other sides in their group before taking on two teams from the opposite group that finished in different positions. The top two teams will contest the gold medal match, while the third- and fourth-placed teams will play for bronze.\n\nA total of 28 matches will be played across the men's and women's tournaments at a purpose-built cricket venue in Pomona. The ICC said details regarding the dates and host of the 2027 ICC Olympics Qualifier will be announced later."
  },
