    "md5": "2edd1a191e78d8afeda055c9dd88d5f6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1841,
    "chunk_text": "Home Lands breaks ground on \u2018Central Park Boulevard Port City Colombo\u2019\n\nFrom left: Amaya Herath, Executive Director of Home Lands Group; Mahela Jayawardene, Home Lands Brand Ambassador; Harsha Amarasekera, Chairman of the Colombo Port City Economic Commission; Dr. Susil Ranasinghe, Minister of Housing, Construction and Water Supply; Nalin Herath, Chairman and Managing Director of Home Lands Group; Duminda Hulangamuwa, Senior Economic Adviser to the President; Eng. L. Kumudu Lal Bogahawatta, Secretary to the Ministry of Housing, Construction and Water Supply; Xiong Hongfeng, Managing Director of CHEC Port City Colombo (Pvt) Ltd; and Harshani Herath, Director of Home Lands Group\n\nHome Lands Group officially commenced construction of Central Park Boulevard Port City Colombo with a ceremonial groundbreaking held at its construction site in Central Park district, Port City Colombo.\n\nThe day\u2019s proceedings began in the morning with the receiving of blessings from religious leaders followed by the laying of the foundation stone and the ceremonial commencement of construction activities in accordance with auspicious times. The evening celebrations brought togetherdistinguished dignitaries including government officials, investors, business leaders, stakeholders, and members of the media to commemorate this significant milestone and celebrate yet another remarkable chapter in the Home Lands journey.\n\nThe ceremonial groundbreaking was officially carried out by distinguished invitees together with the Chairman, and the Management of Home Lands Group, symbolically marking the commencement of construction of Central Park Boulevard Port City Colombo. Beyond breaking ground, the ceremony ushered in a new era for Sri Lanka\u2019s real estate sector and the beginning of what is set to become The Indian Ocean\u2019s Next Wonder."
  },
  {
