    "md5": "44ae84d4ed1d335b5d46f1b039b06829",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1988,
    "chunk_text": "Dr. Rohantha Athukorala awarded Rotarian of the Year\n\nDr. Rohantha Athukorala (left) receives the award from Rotary Sri Lanka and Maldives Governor Delvin Pereira. Rotary International Immediate Past President Stephanie Urchick and Past President/Trustee K.R. Ravindran are also present\n\nDr. Rohantha Athukorala, one of the most respected Rotarians in Sri Lanka and Maldives, was awarded the prestigious \u201cRotarian of the Year 2025/26\u201d award by Governor Delvin Pereira at the Rotary Awards Ceremony, popularly referred to as the \u201cRotary Oscars,\u201d held at ITC Ratnadipa.\n\nThe distinguished global Rotary leaders, present included Immediate Rotary International President Stephanie Urchick and Past Rotary International President/Rotary International Trustee K.R. Ravindran.\n\nThe award recognises Dr. Athukorala\u2019s exceptional contribution to Rotary through his expertise in project management, strategic communications and brand building in which he has consistently helped elevate Rotary\u2019s profile and impact across Sri Lanka and the Maldives.\n\nThis recognition marks the third major Rotary award received by Dr. Athukorala. In 2019, he was honoured as the \u201cMost Outstanding Rotarian of the Year\u201d by then District Governor Dushan Soza. In 2015 Rotary year, Dr. Athukorala was awarded \u201cThe Exceptional Rotarian\u201d under District Governor Gowri Rajan.\n\nIn 2021, he achieved international recognition when Rotary International selected him as one of only six \u201cPeople of Action\u201d honourees worldwide, becoming the first Sri Lankan Rotarian in the country\u2019s history to receive this distinction under the District Governor Ajith Weerasinghe.\n\nBeyond Rotary Dr. Athukorala has an outstanding 21-year career in British multinationals Reckitt Benckiser, Unilever, and DiverseyLever. His area of expertise is in building brands, expanding markets. \u201cThese same skills became a defining factor in his Rotary success,\u201d said Governor Delvin Perera who is a banker by profession."
  },
