    "chunk_size_bytes": 1436,
    "chunk_text": "SriLankan cleared over UAE payment after probe traces cyber attack to recipient\n\nSriLankan Airlines has been cleared of any wrongdoing over a disputed payment to a Dubai-based service provider after investigations established that the funds had been successfully remitted and that the cyber attack originated at the recipient\u2019s end, Ports and Aviation Deputy Minister Janitha Kodithuwakku said.\n\nResponding to questions on the incident, the Deputy Minister said the payment had been classified as successfully completed as the cyber compromise had occurred on the service provider\u2019s side rather than within SriLankan Airlines\u2019 systems.\n\nEarlier, SriLankan Airlines said it had been informed by a service provider in Dubai, United Arab Emirates, that a payment of AED 974,000 had not been received.\n\nSubsequent investigations found that the service provider\u2019s email account had been compromised by a third party, which had altered the beneficiary bank account details. The attackers had also provided the requested supporting documentation through the established official communication channels, misleading SriLankan Airlines into believing it was dealing directly with the legitimate service provider.\n\nThe national carrier maintained that the payment instructions had been manipulated only after the service provider\u2019s email account had been compromised, resulting in the funds being transferred to the altered bank account."
  },
