    "chunk_text": "\u201cEvery time we have visitors, the community provides the food and saves part of the income. That has now become their community fund. They are using it to provide loans to members, buy equipment, from cutlery to pottery, and organise themselves much better, she explained.\n\nEqually important is the investment in human capital. Through education and continuous engagement, villagers have acquired scientific knowledge that enables them to identify mangrove species, monitor flowering and fruiting cycles, collect propagules responsibly and participate actively in ecosystem management.\n\n\u201cNature-based tourism is about working with nature and ensuring that it is in a better condition than when we started. It is not simply using nature for tourism. The goal is to continuously improve the ecosystem while creating sustainable economic opportunities for local communities, she said.\n\nINFRACON 2026 to unite South Asia\u2019s infrastructure and construction industry in Colombo\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
