    "md5": "0a9aac23cae55850e5dbcb0f03926d67",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1671,
    "chunk_text": "EDB hosts regional exporters\u2019 networking forum in Chilaw\n\nThe Sri Lanka Export Development Board (EDB) successfully organized the North Western and North Central Provinces Exporters\u2019 Networking Forum recently at the Nilawin Hotel & Resort in Chilaw.\n\nThe forum was convened under the patronage of Minister of Industry and Entrepreneurship Development Sunil Handunneththi, with the participation of a large number of exporters representing the North Western and North Central Provinces.\n\nThe primary objective of the forum was to enhance regional export capabilities and to establish a direct communication channel between regional exporters, government institutions, and policymakers. The forum served as a vital platform particularly for discussing prevailing challenges related to customs procedures, legal and administrative issues, and market access, while seeking practical solutions to those challenges.\n\nAddressing the exporters at the forum, Minister Sunil Handunneththi emphasized that it is the government\u2019s expectation to resolve, at the earliest, the issues faced by exporters in order to achieve regional export growth. He further stated that this programme aims to strengthen the export sector by gathering new ideas and proposals.\n\nA highlight of the forum was the opportunity extended to participating exporters to engage in direct discussions with representatives of key state institutions, including Sri Lanka Customs and the Inland Revenue Department. Through this engagement, the necessary foundation was laid to connect rural producers with international market linkages, and to build a more equitable export system and a stronger supply chain."
  },
